      <Comment source="BioCyc">This enzyme is involved in carotenoid biosynthesis in plants. Phytoene is converted into &amp;zeta;-carotene as the end product of a two-step desaturation reaction via phytofluene as an intermediate. The enzyme from |FRAME: TAX-1140 &lt;i&gt;Synechococcus elongatus&lt;/i&gt; PCC 7942| can also use NAD+ and NADP+ as electron acceptor. The enzyme from |FRAME: TAX-38851 &lt;i&gt;Gentiana lutea&lt;/i&gt;| shows no activity with NAD+ or NADP+ |CITS: [11714315]|. This is an overall reaction, which is catalyzed in two steps, as follows: |FRAME: RXN-12243 15-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-phytoene + a plastoquinone &amp;rarr; 15,9&apos;-di-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-phytofluene + a plastoquinol| |FRAME: RXN-12244 15,9&apos;-di-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-phytofluene + a plastoquinone &amp;rarr; 9,15,9&apos;-tri-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;zeta;-carotene + a plastoquinol|</Comment>
